---
description: Guardrails for main.ts app wiring
globs: src/main.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

Before editing this file:

1. Read the click listener block end-to-end. It has three branches: block-body click (reveal source), empty-background click (clear both panels), and comment-icon fall-through. Do not add a fourth branch for `.blocklyCommentIcon` that calls `editor.revealRange()` — that closes the bubble.
2. `highlightSubtree` skips the block's next-sibling (`includeNext = false` on root). See AGENTS.md.
3. `lastHighlightedBlockId` is declared once in `startWorkspace` and shared between the forward and reverse sync handlers. Do not redeclare it inside a closure.
4. `clearSelection()` moves the Monaco cursor. Any call site must be wrapped in the `suppressCursorChangesUntil` pattern (`src/editor.ts`) or reverse-sync will re-glow the block that was just cleared.
5. Run `npm run test` after every edit.
